// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// CRAP pins — A RATCHET, NOT A CLIFF. Same contract as .oxlintrc.json:
//
//     every number here HOLDS TODAY (measured by `bun run crap`, both suites);
//     a PR that makes a number achievable lowers it in that same PR;
//     a lowered number never goes back up.
//
// CRAP(m) = cc² · (1 − cov)³ + cc, per function in src/. The target is 7.
// The CI job "CRAP score" fails when any function is above the pin that
// applies to it. Raising `max`, raising an override, or ADDING an override is
// the one change here that needs an argument in the PR description; the
// tool's own NOTE lines say when a number can come down.
//
// `max` is the shared budget — the worst function NOT named below — rather than
// the worst function in the tree, for the reason the lint config gives: a cap
// with slack in it is a cap every other function can grow into. The overrides
// are the outliers that would otherwise set it, one pin each, and the list is
// meant to shrink: an override whose function fits inside `max` is reported as
// stale, and one whose function no longer exists fails the run.
//
// Overrides name a function the way oxlint does. A function oxlint reports
// anonymously shows up as "(anonymous L<line>)", which moves whenever the file
// above it does — so the fix for an anonymous outlier is to name it, not to
// pin it. See CLAUDE.md, "CRAP score".
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
{
  // LOWERED 156 -> 127.82 -> 72 -> 64.57. The convert flow's execFile callback
  // (cc 12 at 0%) set 156; it is now `parseConvertOutput` and friends, pure and
  // unit-tested, the worst of them at 6. Then src/ui/keys/list.ts
  // `handleListNavKeys` (cc 29, 51%) and src/ui/keys/search.ts
  // `handleSearchInputKeys` (cc 27, 49%) set 127.82; both are now dispatch
  // over pure helpers (rowTree.ts, searchEdit.ts) with a unit suite, the worst
  // of them at 7. Then src/clone/run.ts `cancel` (cc 8, never entered) set 72
  // with src/profiles.ts `moveSessionToProfile` (cc 25, 59%) behind it; the
  // first is two named helpers under a stand-in git, the second is the three
  // phases of src/profiles/move.ts, both with a unit suite, the worst at 7.
  // The holder is src/ui/keys/lineEdit.ts `editLine` (cc 18, 47%), with
  // src/ui/keys/clone.ts `handleCloneKeys` at 63.13 behind it.
  "max": 64.57,

  "overrides": [
    // REMOVED: the four src/activity.ts pins (loadCodexActivity 1190,
    // copilotAction 702, codexAction 702, loadCopilotActivity 506). The codex
    // and copilot readers are now src/activity/codex.ts and copilot.ts, walks
    // over small per-record handlers with a unit suite over every tool they
    // render; the worst function in either file is 7.
    //
    // The input-box scan, cc 29 with a quarter of it exercised. In the
    // orchestrator port's area (src/tmux/), so measured here and left alone.
    { "file": "src/tmux/inputBox.ts", "function": "inputRealText", "max": 365.45 }
  ]
}
